On 23 Jun 2005 01:08:11 GMT, anon <anon@anon.com> wrote:

> After losing two more wizards this week to a giant mimic and a rope
> golem, I'm wondering what is the best way to survive a grabbing attack.
> I always start my wizards out with sleep spell, but rope golems are
> sleep resistant, and sleep spell is often useless in close spaces where
> giant mimics are usually found.
> 
> So what is my best option (besides not being grabbed in the first
> place)? Writing Elbereth? (which *never* seems to work when your
> miserable life actually depends on it) Reading a scroll of teleport?
> Prayer? Or are wizards basically screwed once they get grabbed?

Definitely try using the E-word at least once; it's saved my life more
times than I can count. Even if it takes several tries for you to write
it in the dust with your fingers, it just takes one turn for the monster
to see it, let go of you, and allow you to escape; by the time you
encounter such monsters, you should be able to take at least a few hits
from them without dying. If you have an athame or wand of digging (or,
better yet, a wand of fire or lightning for a message that will NEVER
erode*), then use them. Do make sure your character isn't physically or
mentally impaired, though...

(* but can still be erased by other means)

If you don't want to gamble with writing in the dust, self-teleportation
generally works too (as long as you aren't on a no-teleport level). If
you have a wand of teleportation, you can teleport either yourself or
the monster, though if you're facing a large/giant mimic then you're
probably in a shop, where zapping a wand of teleportation could be
rather costly.

Prayer should only be used if your hitpoints are dangerously low (I
forget the thresholds, but the hpmon patch handles this nicely).

All of this should obviously be combined with having a good AC (wear the
best armor you can find that doesn't lower your casting abilities) to
not die immediately, as well as a reasonably powerful attack. Since
you're start-scumming already (for a spellbook of sleep), I suggest you
try for magic missile instead; the spell works wonders, especially if
you can bounce it off a wall - best yet, the rebound won't hurt you at
all if you have magic resistance (which you start with, as well as get
from your quest artifact later).

